{"text":"MODEL_FEEDBACK_JSON:
{
  "positive_alignment_reasons": [
    "Dust Bowl and A New Day Yesterday feel like natural follow-ups to Old Sock and People, Hell & Angels because guitar-driven blues rock is what I want to hear now.",
    "Revelator and the roots-rock choices fit my interest in soulful, song-focused music; melodic classic rock also feels relevant even when it is not my first choice."
  ],
  "negative_misalignment_reasons": [
    "The Endless River shares a broad rock connection, but its atmospheric instrumental direction misses the song-focused listening I want today.",
    "Midwest Farmer's Daughter connects with my occasional country interest, but that connection is less compelling right now than the blues-rock thread in my listening."
  ],
  "overgeneralized_signals": [
    "A broad connection to classic rock does not make every album equally appealing; the blues feel and style of the songs matter more to me today.",
    "My interaction with Blown Away seems to have been given more weight than it deserves as a sign that I currently want country music."
  ],
  "missing_or_underweighted_signals": [
    "The connection between Old Sock and People, Hell & Angels matters because it points toward the guitar-driven blues sound that makes Dust Bowl my strongest choice.",
    "I rarely choose several albums at once, so leaving other appealing records unchosen means I am satisfied with one strong pick, not that those records miss my taste."
  ],
  "summary_diagnosis": "The recommendations mostly understood my blues and roots-rock interests, but stretched that fit too far toward atmospheric rock and country for my mood today."
}"}
